{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's detour is explained by a live LTA advisory, not by choice. EV-ADVIS-02810-01 records a HIGH-severity vehicle fire with all lanes closed on the Ayer Rajah Expressway (AYE) towards Tuas after Clementi Ave 6, active 2026-08-20 20:39:44 to 22:15:24 — a 70.7 minute overlap with this trip's 21:09:44 to 21:50:24 running window — and the same record marks that advisory as intersecting the route the platform booked (intersects_route true, overlaps_trip_window true). The trace's own avoidance of the closure footprint (the derived advisory-area check records 0 fixes inside the advisory geometry) is what routing around a closed segment looks like. That satisfies POL-RD-03 limbs (a), (b) and (c), and by pointing to a specific artifact and a specific clause the driver discharges the burden POL-RD-08 places on him once the rider has shown an excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02810-01", "EV-TRIP-02810", "EV-FARE-02810", "EV-GPS-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Exoneration under POL-RD-03 is capped, and the cap bites here. The justified excess is the lesser of the measured excess and 130% of the additional distance of the shortest lawful alternative plus 1.0 km of tolerance: min(7.2 km, 1.30 x (26.0 - 24.0) + 1.00) = min(7.2, 3.60) = 3.60 km. The closure-adjusted optimal route is therefore trip_record.optimal_distance_km + justified_excess = 24.0 + 3.60 = 27.60 km, with its duration scaled from the booked 32.0 minutes by 27.60/24.0 to 36.8 minutes. Only 3.60 km of the 7.2 km the rider complains of is chargeable to the driver on this clause; every figure comes from the record and none has to be invented.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02810-01", "EV-TRIP-02810", "EV-FARE-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].justified_excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the POL-RD-03 adjustment is made, POL-RD-01 tests the excess that REMAINS, measured on the governing trace figure of 31.2 km: 31.2 - 27.60 = 3.60 km, which is 13.0% of the 27.60 km adjusted optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH limbs to pass — more than 20% of the optimal distance AND more than 0.8 km absolute — and the percentage limb fails, so the route deviation is not established at all. The clause is explicit that where either establishment test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip; the CHARGED fare and the nil refund therefore stand as they are, which is the party-relative effect POL-GEN-03 gives NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02810", "EV-TRIP-02810", "EV-FARE-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].adjusted_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge takes the other view and treats the residual excess as refundable, the quantum is still far below the rider's number. POL-RD-02 directs that where POL-RD-03 excuses part of the excess the recomputation runs against the ADJUSTED optimal route, not the booked one: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 27.60 + 0.28 x 36.8) x the 1.0 surge multiplier recorded on the fare breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 35.604, so the refund is 39.40 - 35.604 = 3.796, payable 3.80 after rounding up to the nearest SGD 0.05. That is 9.6% of charged_total, nowhere near the 90% that would trigger FULL_REFUND, and the 7.85 an unadjusted computation would produce is not available on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02810", "EV-TRIP-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure[0].recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of the distance refund. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines and an ERP and toll total of SGD 0.00, and POL-RD-09(1) provides that off-route pass-through charges are already comprehended in a POL-RD-02 refund, itemised for transparency only and never added to it. There is no separate pass-through or billing-integrity correction to make on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation uplift is available against the driver. The deviation is not MATERIAL on any view: the measured excess of 7.2 km is below the 8.0 km absolute materiality figure and 30.0% is below the 50% percentage figure in POL-RD-01, so the POL-RD-06 profile check is not even engaged. And on the only fields POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit for that test, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 196 completed trips in 90 days (a ratio of 0.0, far below the 0.05 threshold and the 3-flag count), so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies, and no driver-conduct referral arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02810", "EV-GPS-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is unimpaired both at the schema level and under POL-RD-07's own limbs — 100.0% coverage, 245 fixes at a 10 second sample interval, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, all well inside the 90 second, 500 m and 30 second thresholds. The excess and the closure arithmetic therefore rest on clean telemetry, and there is no gap-driven reason to depart from or discount the figures computed on EV-GPS-02810.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02810"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.80,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver.\n\nDISTANCE. The governing measurement is the GPS trace, not the rounded copy on the trip record (POL-RD-01). EV-GPS-02810 records 31.2 km over 245 fixes at a 10-second interval with 100.0% coverage; the booked optimal route is 24.0 km (EV-TRIP-02810). The measured excess is 7.2 km, 30.0% of optimal, so a deviation is established on this trip's own evidence and the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged.\n\nTHE CLOSURE. EV-ADVIS-02810-01 is a genuine LTA advisory (weight 1.0, COMPLETE): a vehicle fire closing all lanes on the Ayer Rajah Expressway towards Tuas after Clementi Ave 6, active 2026-08-20 20:39:44 to 22:15:24, intersecting the booked route (intersects_route true, overlaps_trip_window true) and covering the trip window 21:09:44 to 21:50:24. The trace never enters the closed area (0 fixes inside it, closest approach 1,699 m), i.e. the actual route left the optimal corridor around the affected segment rather than driving through it. POL-RD-03 limbs (a) to (c) are therefore met. The rider's argument that the trace's avoidance of the closed area defeats limb (c) is rejected: avoiding the affected segment is precisely what limb (c) requires. The driver's contrary suggestion that the adjustment leaves no deviation at all is also rejected: the deviation is established on the measured excess of 7.2 km / 30.0%, and POL-RD-03 directs the excess beyond its cap to be refunded through POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal; it is the MATERIALITY test that is assessed on the excess remaining, and here the remaining excess is not material.\n\nTHE CAP. The justified excess is min(7.2, 1.30 x (26.0 - 24.0) + 1.00) = 3.60 km. The closure-adjusted optimal distance is 24.0 + 3.60 = 27.60 km, and its duration is 32.0 x 27.60/24.0 = 36.8 min.\n\nTHE REFUND. EV-FARE-02810 records fare_model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not run and POL-RD-02 governs; the surge multiplier, read from the fare breakdown, is 1.0. Against the closure-adjusted optimal the recomputed fare is (3.80 + 0.75 x 27.60 + 0.28 x 36.8) x 1.0 + 0.80 = 35.604. The charged total is 39.40. The refund is 39.40 - 35.604 = 3.796, rounded up to SGD 3.80. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 3.80.\n\nOTHER POINTS. No part of the excess is a rider-requested detour: EV-CHAT-02810 holds no messages and no waypoint hint, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable and its corroboration test cannot be run. No endpoint was amended (POL-RD-05) and the trip is not pooled (RYDE_X, POL-RD-12), so the booked optimal of 24.0 km is the correct starting baseline. EV-FARE-02810 carries no gantry lines and no airport surcharge, so nothing is added on top of the distance refund and POL-RD-09(1) is respected. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s, 10 s sampling), so no escalation is available on that ground. The driver's profile shows 0 deviation flags in 90 days against 196 completed trips, so no POL-RD-06 pattern is established and no driver-conduct referral arises; in any event the excess is not material. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires, and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect of SGD 3.80 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this ruling is executed automatically. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
